  "markdown": "Material family\n\n# Grasscloth and natural weaves\n\nSisal, raffia, grass and other weaves. Colour and texture move from roll to roll.\n\n![Close detail of a woven grasscloth wallcovering turning an external corner, the weave running straight and tight to the edge.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-residences-06-800.webp)\n\nA woven grasscloth turning an external corner at the Four Seasons residences, Ten Trinity Square. The close view shows the natural fibre and the finished edge.Mr Wallcover project photograph.[Four Seasons: the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\nBefore you choose\n\n**Consider it when**\n: Natural fibre and a visible panel character are part of the look you want.\n\n**The trade-off**\n: Adjacent drops can differ in shade; do not expect an invisible joint.\n\n**Before ordering**\n: Review a full-wall example, panel layout and the exact care sheet.\n\n01 · The finish\n\n## Joins\n\nSeams show. The direction of the weave is agreed before the first length is cut.\n\n02 · The setting\n\n## Where it belongs\n\nRooms where variation is wanted\n\n03 · Installation\n\n## Handling\n\nClean hands, an adhesive that suits the backing, and enough length from one batch to keep a wall together.\n\n04 · Living with it\n\n## Care\n\nDry and gentle. Adhesive on the face marks the weave. Not a washable surface.\n\nDigital colour is a guide. Order a cutting or a sample before you commit to a room. Some makers’ own sample routes are listed under [official buying routes](https://www.mrwallcover.com/buying-routes/). We can install material you have already bought, or source a family and install it. Either way, the next step is a short note about the room.\n\nBefore you order\n\n## For a high-value order\n\n- Workmanship is guaranteed for twelve months. [The aftercare page](https://www.mrwallcover.com/aftercare/) sets out what is covered.\n- Public liability, employers' liability and professional indemnity details are available on request.\n- Risk assessments and method statements (RAMS) on every job, with Dorin Burcus supervising on site.\n- A core team of six wallpaper hangers and six decorators who work together every day, scaling to 25–35 skilled tradespeople for large hotel programmes.\n- [For designers and architects](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/designers/)\n- [Download the specification schedule (CSV)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/downloads/wallcovering-specification-schedule.csv)\n- [Trade and contractors](https://www.mrwallcover.com/trade/)\n\nIllustrative material study · confirm the actual finish with a sample\n\nPause motion\n\nSave to shortlist\n\nSaved on this device only.\n\n[Discuss this material](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=source&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Agrasscloth-and-weaves) [I already have it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Agrasscloth-and-weaves)\n\n[How we install it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/grasscloth-installation/)\n\nInstallation experience\n\n## On the record\n\nAt [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/) we hung Phillip Jeffries Tweed and Omexco between 2016 and 2019, with shading on the natural textiles checked continuously so the walls read as a single surface. At [The Biltmore Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/biltmore-mayfair/), the 2018 guest-room programme of more than 15,000 m² included a Phillip Jeffries schedule.\n\nThe [grasscloth guide](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/grasscloth-seams-and-variation/) explains what is normal and what is a fault, and [grasscloth installation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/grasscloth-installation/) explains how we set out and shade a room.\n\nPlan the detail\n\n## Useful reading\n\n- [Choosing wallcoverings](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/choosing-wallcoverings/)\n- [Grasscloth seams and variation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/grasscloth-seams-and-variation/)\n\nFrom our projects\n\n## Selected work\n\n- [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n- [The Biltmore Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/biltmore-mayfair/)\n- [Brown's Hotel, Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n- [Raffles London at The OWO, Whitehall](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/raffles-london-the-owo/)\n\nMakers installed\n\n## Grasscloth and natural weaves: makers we have hung\n\nEach in our own photograph of its product on the wall. Naming a maker records an installation, not an endorsement.\n\n- ![Close-up of a woven, natural-texture Phillip Jeffries wallcovering, the Millennium Hotel, Grosvenor Square, now The Biltmore Mayfair.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/biltmore-04-800.webp)\n\n### Phillip Jeffries\n\nInstalled at [The Biltmore Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/biltmore-mayfair/) · [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/).\n\n- ![Close-up of a pale check Omexco wallcovering, a private project, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/brand-omexco-01-800.webp)\n\n### Omexco\n\nInstalled at a private project, London, 2017. [See the post](https://www.instagram.com/p/BaCaL9JAVaV/).\n\nGrasscloth and natural weaves: send a short note about the room, or tell us you already have the material.\n\n[Discuss this material](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=source&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Agrasscloth-and-weaves) [I already have it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Agrasscloth-and-weaves)\n\n[How we install grasscloth and natural weaves](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/grasscloth-installation/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder\n",
